   "hypothesis_id": "hyp3",
   "mechanism": "Dominant‑negative LMNA variants disrupt the nuclear lamina, making cardiomyocyte nuclei mechanically fragile. Repeated contraction‑induced nuclear stress leads to DNA damage, apoptosis, and replacement fibrosis, which weakens the ventricular wall and dilates the chamber. This is a distinct mechanism from sarcomere defects, explaining the earlier arrhythmias and faster progression seen in laminopathies.",
